{"type":"text","text":"Done. Mapping sheet 3, scene: first overworld screen of Zelda, no reference used. All five discoveries are recorded and promoted.\n\n## Addresses found\n\n| Value | Address | Encoding |\n|---|---|---|\n| Rupee count | **`$067D`** | 1 byte binary 0–255, drawn as decimal in the top HUD counter |\n| Key count | **`$066E`** | 1 byte binary, middle HUD counter |\n| Bomb count | **`$0658`** | 1 byte binary, bottom HUD counter |\n| Heart meter | **`$066F`** | packed: high nibble = (containers − 1), low nibble = (whole hearts − 1) |\n| Heart fill | **`$0670`** | fill of the rightmost heart: `$00` empty, `$01–$7F` half, `$80–$FF` full |\n\n## How, and what the proof screenshots showed\n\n**Hearts** — differential search: snapshot → Octorok hit (3→2 hearts) → snapshot gave **144** `decreased` survivors; a clean single hit on the tree screen gave **23**; intersecting both left **10**; the next (fatal) hit left **4** (`$0439`, `$043A`, `$066F`, `$0670`). Writing `$0439/$043A` did nothing, so `$066F` was isolated.\n- Screenshots: `$066F=0x22` → **3 full hearts**; `$066F=0x42,$0670=0xFF` → **3 filled + 2 empty outline hearts** (5 containers); `$066F=0x44,$0670=0xFF` → **5 full hearts**; `$066F=0x22,$0670=0x40` → **2 full + 1 half heart**.\n\n**Rupees/keys/bombs** — I traced the HUD routine (PCs `$6CCE–$6D43`), which draws counters from `$066D/$066E/$0664/$0658` and `$066F/$0670`, every 2 frames; its disassembly shows `DEC $067D`/`DEC $067E` on a spend/use. Then, from a clean `load_state`, writing `$067D=4`, `$066E=8`, `$0658=9` and waiting gave a screenshot with the HUD reading **`X4` (rupee), `X8` (key), `X9` (bomb)**. The nametable confirmed the digits (tile 4 at row 3 col 13; tile 8 at row 5; tile 9 at row 6), and the CHR-RAM icons confirmed row 5 is a **key** and row 6 is a **bomb** (circle + fuse).\n\nNote on mechanism: the heart meter is redrawn continuously (writes appear within ~2 frames), while the rupee/key/bomb digits are redrawn on an event — a bare write to the rupee sometimes needs a HUD refresh to show, which is why the earlier isolated `$067D` write looked inert.\n\nRecorded with `source: \"differential search\"` and promoted to `mappings/sha1-799459548f9636dd263200da494f04058f5540e2.json` (now 8 addresses). The emulator was returned to the clean save (`file A`, 3 hearts, 0/0/0)."}
